A||||6||jhar1987||duke codes 33,34,35?||||9||
Z||000000||jhar1987||04-12-2000||07:38 PM||||my duke is driving me crazy!!!!! I need to know where to go from here. I have replaced all the sensors, the manifold differential pressure, idle air control valve,trottle position,every thing and it still doesn't run right. Even reset the ecm.||||reg||9
Z||000001||theogre||04-12-2000||07:51 PM||||You need to hook up an ECM scanner and read the sensors while running. One of the new sensors may be bad or you may have an ECM with problems. (A common ECM problem is cracked solder joints between the circuit board and the main connectors to the wiring harness.)<P>On the other hand you could have a bad/jammed EGR valve. A vac leak. A bad vapor recovery can. a bad brake booster(which will often cause a vacuum leak). A fuel pressure/injector problem. <p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 04-12-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||jhar1987||04-12-2000||08:08 PM||||thanks ogre, i guess i will try the scanner. I disconnected the brake booster and vac. can to see if she would do any better there was no difference. thanks again||||reg||1
Z||000003||Ozzy||04-13-2000||12:08 AM||||I'm trying to remember...I can tell you that I went thru a period of "hell" with my "duke" too. (Ogre can probably remember me bugging him about it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> )I did most everything too. The damn thing kept running in open loop. So I rebuilt the TBI, put a new injector and swapped out the O2 sensor. Has been running like a clock ever since.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Ozzy||||reg||1
Z||000004||Phil||04-13-2000||07:56 AM||||Running like a clock- you mean with a constant ticking noise?||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||04-13-2000||10:01 AM||||Definatly scan it. Even tho you replaced everything you could still have a bad wire or cruddy connection.<P>there will be a new "HOW TO:" posted in a bit about the TPS. There is a quality issue with the company who actually makes these. <P>Doesn't matter where you get them they all likely will show a makermark of CTS on the shell some place. At least this is true for the 700 tbi. Knowing the industry I expect it's true of the 300 TBI and V6 as well.<P>I've been thru 3 of the damn things in a year. one died in 18,000 miles, one was defective out of the box. Finally got one that's good. at least so far. It was a CTS marked one but I got it thru Borg-Warner. So there may be levels of QA that the real maker is using where less tested lots got to the cheaper distributors.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Ozzy||04-13-2000||10:25 AM||||Hey Phil...Yoo are a Funny guy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Actually that is deeper than I considered before using that analogy! Ticking and reliable...as for the V-6 so far????<P><BR>Ozzy||||reg||1
